      "description": "Third Coast Infrastructure is a Houston-headquartered offshore and coastal midstream platform operating natural gas, crude oil and NGL gathering, transmission, processing and floating-production infrastructure across the U.S. Gulf Coast and Gulf of Mexico. The platform traces to American Midstream Partners, was taken private by ArcLight Energy Partners Fund V in 2019, added J.P. Morgan Asset Management's Infrastructure Investments Fund as a significant minority co-owner in 2021, and moved ArcLight's remaining 25.1% interest into ArcLight 3C SPV in July 2022. Current public materials list Third Coast CV as an ArcLight investment and identify a J.P. Morgan Asset Management-advised vehicle as an owner; exact current parent-platform ownership percentages are not publicly disclosed. As of May 2026, company materials described approximately 1,900 pipeline miles, one gas processing plant and interests in four offshore floating production systems. No platform-level exit or signed pending ownership transfer was identified through August 15, 2026.",
